---
title: Battle of the Counties — California's Civics & Esports Competition
description: >-
  Battle of the Counties is a statewide civics and academic esports competition for California K-12 students, running from September qualifiers to the January 9, 2027 Statewide Championship.
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block head %}
<style>
  /* ── HERO OVERRIDES ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .page-hero-eyebrow {
    font-size: 20px; color: var(--red);
  }

  /* ── MAP PANEL (right side of hero) ──────────────────────────── */
  .botc-map {
    padding: 56px 48px;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-self: stretch;
  }
  .botc-map-lbl {
    font-family: 'Pixelify Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;
    color: rgba(139,163,194,0.6); letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 24px; text-align: center;
  }
  .botc-map .ca-map { width: 100%; max-width: 430px; height: auto; display: block; margin: 0 auto; }
  @media (max-width: 768px) { .botc-map { display: none; } }

  /* ── ENTRY STEPS ────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .entry-intro { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--civic); max-width: 600px; margin-bottom: 3.5rem; }
  .entry-note {
    margin-top: 40px; padding: 24px 32px;
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(22,43,77,0.8); border-left: 4px solid var(--red);
    display: flex; gap: 24px; align-items: start;
  }
  .entry-note-lbl {
    font-family: 'Pixelify Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--red);
    white-space: nowrap; padding-top: 2px;
  }
  .entry-note-body { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--civic); }

  /* ── CRITERIA ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .criteria-intro { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--gray); max-width: 600px; margin-bottom: 3.5rem; }

  /* ── ABOUT BLURB ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .about-blurb {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 64px; align-items: start;
  }
  .about-blurb-body { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--gray); }
  .about-blurb-body a { color: var(--ink); }

  /* ── RESPONSIVE ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .about-blurb { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .entry-note { flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
    .entry-note-lbl { white-space: normal; }
  }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<!-- HERO -->
<div class="page-hero">
  <div class="page-hero-content">
    <div class="page-hero-eyebrow">Battle of the Counties</div>
    <h1 class="page-hero-h1">Game&#8209;Based Civics &amp; Community&#8209;Based Learning for California&nbsp;K–12</h1>
    <p class="page-hero-sub">
      A statewide civics and esports competition. Student teams investigate a real community challenge, design a solution in Minecraft Education, and pitch it to the leaders who can act on it.
    </p>
    <div class="page-hero-cta">
      <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScQ_Ey7Yax2ZY4iL5g_nlhYBC94LgoUUhQJX_KQA50Rpbvv8g/viewform?usp=header" target="_blank" class="btn-nav-red">Register a Team</a>
      <a href="#enter" class="btn-ghost-civic">How to Enter →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="botc-map">
    {% include "partials/california-map.njk" %}
  </div>
</div>

<!-- DATE TICKER -->
<div class="ticker">
  <div class="ticker-lbl">Key Dates</div>
  <div class="ticker-items">
    <div class="ticker-event"><span class="ticker-date">SEPT 22</span><span class="ticker-name">World goes live</span></div>
    <div class="ticker-event"><span class="ticker-date">NOV 15</span><span class="ticker-name">Submissions close</span></div>
    <div class="ticker-event"><span class="ticker-date">DEC 4–5</span><span class="ticker-name">County Finals</span></div>
    <div class="ticker-event"><span class="ticker-date">JAN 9, 2027</span><span class="ticker-name">Statewide Championship</span></div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- THREE ROUNDS -->
<section class="sec sec-cream">
  <div class="sec-header">
    <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-dark page-h2">Three rounds of competition.</h2>
    <p class="sec-header-intro">
      Teams advance from virtual qualifiers to live county championships, then compete for the statewide title. Each round raises the stakes, and the size of the audience with them.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid-3">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-eyebrow card-eyebrow-dark">Round 01</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">Virtual Qualifiers</h3>
      <div class="card-badge">Opens Sept 22</div>
      <p class="card-body">Teams explore their county's Minecraft Education world, investigate a real local challenge, and build their solution. Submit a 3-minute video walkthrough before November 15. Judges select the top teams from each county to advance.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-eyebrow card-eyebrow-dark">Round 02</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">County Finals</h3>
      <div class="card-badge">Dec 4–5</div>
      <p class="card-body">Top teams compete live at their county office of education. Timed build events, presentations to judges and local civic leaders. County Champions are crowned by grade level.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card card-champ">
      <div class="card-eyebrow card-eyebrow-light">Round 03</div>
      <h3 class="card-title card-title-light">Statewide Championship</h3>
      <div class="card-badge card-badge-red">Jan 9, 2027</div>
      <p class="card-body card-body-light">County Champions face off at the Richard Nixon Presidential Library in Yorba Linda. Projects are presented to state educators, community leaders, and real decision-makers. This is what it's all for.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- HOW TO ENTER -->
<section id="enter" class="sec sec-navy">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-light page-h2 h2-body">How to enter.</h2>
  <p class="entry-intro">
    Every participating school fields one team of four students. No prior Minecraft experience is needed. The worlds come built, and your educators get training and support before the world goes live.
  </p>
  <div class="grid-4">
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">01</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Form a Team</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Recruit four students from your school. One team per school enters the qualifier.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">02</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Explore the World</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Starting September 22, your team enters your county's Minecraft Education world and investigates a real local challenge.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">03</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Design &amp; Build</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Design a solution to the challenge and build it in Minecraft Education. Every block should serve a purpose.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">04</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Submit by Nov 15</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Record a 3-minute walkthrough of your build. Submit your entry before the November 15 deadline.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="entry-note">
    <div class="entry-note-lbl">Participating Counties</div>
    <p class="entry-note-body">Orange County (lead), San Bernardino County, Riverside County, and Yolo County are participating in the 2026–27 program year. More counties are expected to join as the program grows.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHAT MAKES A STRONG ENTRY -->
<section class="sec sec-cream">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-dark page-h2 h2-body">What judges look for.</h2>
  <p class="criteria-intro">
    Judges look at the full arc from investigation to solution. A strong entry shows the community thinking behind every design decision, which matters more than how impressive the build looks.
  </p>
  <div class="grid-4">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-eyebrow card-eyebrow-red">Research</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">Investigate Before You Build</h3>
      <p class="card-body">Strong entries show real investigation: listening to community voices, understanding the challenge, and grounding decisions in evidence.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-eyebrow card-eyebrow-red">Solution</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">Design That Responds</h3>
      <p class="card-body">The solution should answer a real community need. Creativity helps, but the ideas that hold up are the ones rooted in what the team learned.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-eyebrow card-eyebrow-red">Build</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">Every Block Has a Purpose</h3>
      <p class="card-body">The Minecraft Education build is how judges see your thinking. Every block should show purpose, not just polish.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-eyebrow card-eyebrow-red">Communication</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">Make the Case</h3>
      <p class="card-body">Your 3-minute walkthrough should explain what you investigated, what you designed, and why it would improve the community.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- REGISTER CTA BAND -->
<div class="cta-band">
  <div class="cta-band-inner">
    <h2 class="cta-band-h2">Ready to compete?</h2>
    <p class="cta-band-body">
      The world opens September 22. Get your team together, explore your county, and submit your entry before November 15.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-band-btns">
      <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScQ_Ey7Yax2ZY4iL5g_nlhYBC94LgoUUhQJX_KQA50Rpbvv8g/viewform?usp=header" target="_blank" class="btn-white">Register a Team</a>
      <a href="/educators/" class="btn-ghost-white">For Educators →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ABOUT LEVELUP CIVICS -->
<section class="sec sec-cream">
  <div class="about-blurb">
    <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-dark page-h2">About LevelUp Civics</h2>
    <div>
      <p class="about-blurb-body">
        Level Up Civics Foundation is a California nonprofit reimagining civic education through game-based community design. Battle of the Counties is our flagship program — a statewide competition where K-12 students investigate real challenges in their own communities, build solutions in Minecraft Education, and present them to the leaders who can act on their ideas.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <a href="/about/" class="btn-outline">Learn more about us →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- PARTNERS BAR -->
<div class="partners-bar">
  <div class="partners-lbl">In Partnership With</div>
  <div class="partners-names">
    <span class="partner">Orange County Dept. of Education</span>
    <span class="partner">San Bernardino COE</span>
    <span class="partner">Riverside COE</span>
    <span class="partner">Yolo COE</span>
    <span class="partner">Lifeboat Studios</span>
  </div>
</div>

{% endblock %}
